  "about": {
    "description": "cUSDO is the ERC-4626 tokenized vault wrapper of USDO issued by OpenEden Digital, structured as a Bermuda Monetary Authority licensed segregated accounts company. Unlike USDO which distributes yield through positive rebases of the token balance, cUSDO is a non-rebasing share token where value accrues through a rising convertToAssets rate against the underlying USDO. This makes cUSDO more compatible with DeFi venues that assume constant token balances, such as lending markets, DEX liquidity pools, and structured products. Every cUSDO share is redeemable for its proportional amount of USDO in the vault, and the underlying reserves inherit the tokenized US Treasury bill backing and Chainlink Proof of Reserve attestation of the base USDO layer.",
